            <ArticleTitle>The use of clonidine for the treatment of meperidine withdrawal in a multidisciplinary pain program setting. A case presentation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>72-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The management of iatrogenic drug dependence in individuals with pain can be more difficult than the treatment of the pain itself. In addition to a multidisciplinary approach to the treatment of a patient with chronic pain, there is a need for a rapid, safe, and effective method of detoxification from opiate use. Clonidine HCl, a nonopiate, has been found, in this case presentation, to be a valuable option.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
